    {
      "text": "Hochschild and cyclic homology of quantum groups — For an arbitrary complex linear semisimple Lie group G, we consider Hopf algebras of the deformations of the formal and algebraic functions on G.\n\n**Hochschild and cyclic homology of quantum groups**\n\n*Ping Feng1'* and Boris Tsygan2'***\n\n42 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For an arbitrary complex linear semisimple Lie group G, we consider Hopf algebras of the deformations of the formal and algebraic functions on G. The Hochschild and cyclic homology of these Hopf algebras are computed when the value of the deformation parameter is generic. Table of Contents\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; © Springer-Verlag; 1 Introduction; 2 Definitions of Hochschild and Cyclic Homolog; 3 Quantum Groups; 4 A Spectral Sequence; 5 The Lie Algebra Homology; 5.1 Formal Functions; 6 Hochschild and Cyclic Homology of Quantum Gr; 6.1 Quantum Formal Groups; 6.2 Quantum Algebraic Groups; Appendix B Example G = SL(2, C)",
